+### Transferring a user to another organization
+
+`POST /orgs/{orgID}/users/{uid}/transfer` with `{"toOrgId":"globex"}` moves a
+user (for example between group companies).
+
+- Only org admins of the organization in the path may transfer its users (else 403).
+  The organization must be the caller's own; another one → 404.
+- The user must belong to the organization in the path (else 404).
+- The target organization must exist and differ from the current one. An
+  organization exists when at least one user belongs to it (there is no
+  organizations table); a missing target → 400, the same one → 400.
+- The user leaves the organization's projects: their memberships are removed,
+  the tasks assigned to them are unassigned, and the org admin flag is cleared.
+- If the user is a member of an archived project → 409 (archived projects
+  reject all writes, so the membership cannot be removed).
+
